# Shared Types — Contract Rules

## The Rule

Types in `src/types/shared/` are the **contract** between the three independent deployables. They must be identical across all three folders. Any change to a shared type must be made in all three in a single commit.

```
api/src/types/shared/          ← authoritative source
dashboard/src/types/shared/    ← identical copy
extension/src/types/shared/    ← identical copy
```

## Core Shared Type Files

```
mode.types.ts         → ModeType, Mode, ModeSession, ModeSessionStatus
download.types.ts     → Download, DownloadStatus, DownloadHealth
metrics.types.ts      → UserMetrics, ModeTimeEntry, DailyActivity, StreakData
user.types.ts         → User (public shape only — no password, no tokens)
tab.types.ts          → TabEvent, BrowsingSession
ai.types.ts           → AIInsight, InsightType, NudgeType
websocket.types.ts    → all WebSocket event payload shapes
```

## Type Definitions

```typescript
// mode.types.ts
export enum ModeType {
  DEV       = 'dev',
  CHILL     = 'chill',
  DEEP_WORK = 'deep_work',
  STUDY     = 'study',
  CUSTOM    = 'custom',
}

export interface Mode {
  id:                 string
  userId:             string
  name:               string
  type:               ModeType
  color:              string          // hex #RRGGBB
  pinnedTabs:         string[]        // URLs
  blockedDomains:     string[]
  focusTimerMinutes:  number | null
  isActive:           boolean
  createdAt:          string          // ISO string — not Date (JSON-safe)
  updatedAt:          string
}

export interface ModeSession {
  id:          string
  userId:      string
  modeId:      string
  modeName:    string
  modeColor:   string
  startedAt:   string                 // ISO string
  endedAt:     string | null          // null = currently active
  durationMs:  number | null          // null = currently active
  focusScore:  number | null          // 0–100, null if not yet calculated
}

// metrics.types.ts
export interface UserMetrics {
  userId:         string
  updatedAt:      string
  streak: {
    current:      number
    longest:      number
    lastActiveDate: string
  }
  today: {
    downloads:    number
    newFiles:     number
    duplicates:   number
    focusScore:   number | null
    activeMinutes: number
  }
  week: {
    downloads:    number
    newFiles:     number
    duplicates:   number
    topMode:      string | null
    peakHour:     number | null       // 0–23
    peakDay:      string | null       // 'Mon'–'Sun'
  }
  modeTime:       ModeTimeEntry[]
}

export interface ModeTimeEntry {
  modeId:         string
  modeName:       string
  modeColor:      string
  totalMinutes:   number
  percentage:     number
}

// websocket.types.ts — all WS event shapes
export interface WsMetricsDelta {
  type:       'metrics:updated'
  userId:     string
  delta: Partial<UserMetrics['today']>
}

export interface WsDownloadNew {
  type:       'download:new'
  userId:     string
  download:   Download
}

export interface WsInsightNew {
  type:       'insight:new'
  userId:     string
  insight:    AIInsight
}

export type WsEvent = WsMetricsDelta | WsDownloadNew | WsInsightNew
```

## API Response Envelope

```typescript
// All API responses use this envelope — defined in shared types
export interface ApiSuccess<T> {
  success: true
  data:    T
}

export interface ApiError {
  success: false
  error: {
    code:    string
    message: string
    issues?: unknown[]    // Zod validation issues
  }
}

export type ApiResponse<T> = ApiSuccess<T> | ApiError
```

## No Database Types in Shared

```typescript
// ✅ Shared types are plain data shapes — no Mongoose, no ObjectId
export interface User {
  id:    string      // string — not mongoose.Types.ObjectId
  email: string
}

// ❌ Never leak Mongoose types into shared
import { Document } from 'mongoose'
export interface User extends Document { }  // WRONG — extension/dashboard don't have mongoose
```

## Dates as ISO Strings

```typescript
// ✅ All dates in shared types are ISO strings — JSON-safe, works in all three contexts
createdAt: string    // "2026-03-05T14:30:00.000Z"

// ❌ Never use Date objects in shared types — they don't survive JSON serialization
createdAt: Date      // becomes string in JSON anyway — be explicit
```
